### FastMediatR Sample API — HTTP test file
### Run the API first:  dotnet run --project samples/FastMediatR.Sample.Api
### (or use the start-web-api.cmd helper in the repo root)
###
### Default URL (http profile):  http://localhost:5100
### See ../../docs/260524_1300-fastmediatr-usage-guide.md for what each behavior does.
###
### VS Code REST Client extension:  https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=humao.rest-client
### JetBrains HTTP Client:          supported natively in Rider / ReSharper

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5100

### Reusable ids ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A non-empty user id (any non-empty Guid resolves to a sample user on GET).
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
# The empty Guid is treated as "not found" by GetUserByIdQueryHandler.
@emptyUserId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HEALTH
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Health check — liveness probe
# Expected: 200 OK  { "status": "ok", "phase": "Phase 6" }
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COMMANDS
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Create user — CreateUserCommand : IRequest<Guid>
# Flow: LoggingBehavior → PerformanceBehavior → ValidationBehavior → NoOpSampleBehavior → handler
# Expected: 201 Created  { "id": "<guid>" }  with Location: /users/<guid>
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "displayName": "Alice"
}

###

### Create user — VALIDATION FAILURE (invalid email)
# ValidationBehavior runs CreateUserCommandValidator and throws ValidationException.
# Expected: 400 Bad Request  problem+json with errors["Email"]
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "displayName": "Bob"
}

###

### Create user — VALIDATION FAILURE (empty display name)
# Expected: 400 Bad Request  problem+json with errors["DisplayName"]
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "carol@example.com",
  "displayName": ""
}

###

### Create user — VALIDATION FAILURE (multiple errors)
# Expected: 400 Bad Request  problem+json with errors for both Email and DisplayName
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "",
  "displayName": ""
}

###

### Deactivate user — DeactivateUserCommand : IRequest (void / Unit)
# Handler uses [HandlerLifetime(Transient)] to demonstrate per-handler lifetime override.
# Expected: 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# QUERIES
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Get user by id — GetUserByIdQuery : IRequest<UserDto?>  (found)
# Any non-empty Guid resolves to a sample user.
# Expected: 200 OK  { "id": "<guid>", "email": "sample@example.com", "displayName": "Sample User" }
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Get user by id — NOT FOUND (empty Guid → handler returns null)
# Expected: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{emptyUserId}}
Accept: application/json

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTIFICATIONS
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Publish user-created notification — UserCreatedNotification (parallel fan-out)
# Uses the default TaskWhenAllPublisher; all INotificationHandler<UserCreatedNotification>
# subscribers run concurrently. The `email` value is passed as a query-string parameter.
# Expected: 202 Accepted
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/events/created?email=alice@example.com

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TELEMETRY DEMO
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Telemetry demo — Send (traced) + Publish (untraced)
# Dispatches a GetUserByIdQuery (emits a "GetUserByIdQuery" span via TracingBehavior)
# and publishes a UserCreatedNotification. Spans are written to the console exporter.
# Expected: 200 OK  { "span": "GetUserByIdQuery", "found": false, "notificationPublished": true }
GET {{baseUrl}}/telemetry/demo
Accept: application/json
